  "overview": {
    "title": "Clay, green glaze and manuscripts",
    "p1": "Tamegroute is a small Draa village known across Morocco for its green-glazed pottery and for the zaouia’s historic library of manuscripts.",
    "p2": "You can watch potters at work, browse ceramics, and — when access allows — see the library’s collection of religious and scientific texts. It is a culture stop rather than a sand or dune day.",
    "p3": "Go with respect for religious spaces, ask before photographing people at work, and leave time for the road back to Zagora."
  },
